{% comment %}
  The polling endpoint supplies arrays and a valid focus. Keep older or
  incomplete payloads usable as well; unknown focus falls back to news.
{% endcomment %}
{% unless schedule %}{% assign schedule = "" | split: "," %}{% endunless %}
{% unless news %}{% assign news = "" | split: "," %}{% endunless %}
{% case focus %}
  {% when "news", "result", "standings", "grid", "schedule" %}
  {% else %}{% assign focus = "news" %}
{% endcase %}

{% comment %}
  Secondary labels are gray only on the 2-bit and 4-bit palettes, the ones
  with real gray ink. Elsewhere they stay black: a 1-bit screen dithers gray
  text into speckle (TRMNL's reviewers flag it), and so does every colour
  palette, which has no gray and no prefix to override it with.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  Reusable blocks for the four layouts. The payload is built by
  apps/web/src/lib/trmnl/payload.ts and is fully formatted there:
  times are already in the owner's zone and language, so nothing here does
  date arithmetic. Liquid computing "time until" would freeze whenever the
  payload is unchanged, because TRMNL skips the redraw.
  This file defines partials only. Each of the four view files supplies its
  own layout container; wrapping these definitions in a layout would nest it.
  All images use image-dither for consistent platform palette handling.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  `w--full`: TRMNL's value fitting shrinks the value to its parent's width,
  and in a centred flex column that parent is otherwise exactly as wide as the
  text, so a long winner's name never shrank.
{% endcomment %}
{% template lead %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall w--full">
  <span class="title {{ label_size | default: 'lg:title--large' }}">{{ lead.label }}</span>
  <span class="value {{ size }}" data-value-fit="true">{{ lead.value }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  Flag, race name, circuit, then round and dates. The full layout can combine
  the circuit and round/date line; half screens put the flag beside the name
  and the details below. The flag is decoration: in grayscale Italy, Ireland
  and Mexico are the same three stripes, so it can never be the only thing that
  says which race this is.

  `name_size` is the race name's size, `detail_size` the circuit and round's,
  and `flag_size` sets the flag's height, matched to the text beside it on OG
  and X. Its width follows the flag's shape, capped for Qatar, whose file's
  viewBox is 75:18 and stretches to fit.
  Widths over 128px use the named scale (`lg:w--max-48` is 192px): the
  Framework only generates bracketed sizes up to `[128px]`, and a larger one
  silently does nothing, which squeezed every flag on the X into the OG's cap.
  `shrink-0` keeps the shape in a narrow column, where flex shrank the width
  and not the height.

  Nothing is clamped: an ellipsis cut the dates off. The dates never split
  ("1 – 3 May"): their spaces become non-breaking here, because the Framework's
  label is a flex container that swallowed the space before a nested no-wrap
  span, and it has no text no-wrap class.

  The circuit and round are black, not gray: on the X, gray small labels
  were too faint to read at arm's length, and size alone already sets them
  below the name.

  One flag image uses responsive sizing and `image-dither` for TRMNL's
  palette conversion on every device. The frame is a black
  box with 2px of padding (`bg--black p--0.5`), so white fields (Japan,
  Monaco, Poland) keep an edge against the screen. It was an inline border,
  but TRMNL's rules forbid inline styles, and the Framework has no all-sides
  border class; 2px is its smallest padding step.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
  Between rounds (`between_rounds`), in the lead's place: this Grand Prix and
  the rounds after it, each with its dates, up to `limit`. A session time
  weeks ahead was the screen's biggest type ("Free Practice 1, Fri 25 Sept,
  9:30"); the dates say when the weekend is, and the timeline below says the
  rest. `size` is the table's size and `title_size` the heading's.
  The round and dates never wrap. `stacked` puts them under the name, for the
  portrait OG's narrow slots, where one row of three wrapped every name.
{% endcomment %}
{% template upcoming %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--stretch-x gap--xsmall w--full">
  <span class="title {{ title_size }}">Coming up</span>
  {% if stacked %}
  <div class="flex flex--col flex--stretch-x gap--xsmall">
    {% for round in upcoming limit: limit %}
    <div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
      <span class="title title--small">{{ round.short_name }}</span>
      <span class="label label--small">R{{ round.round }} · {{ round.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" | replace: "–", "&#8288;–&#8288;" }}</span>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <table class="table w--full {{ size }}">
    <tbody>
      {% for round in upcoming limit: limit %}
      <tr>
        <td class="w--0"><span class="label lg:label--large pr--2">R{{ round.round }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="title title--small lg:title--base pr--2">{{ round.short_name }}</span></td>
        <td class="w--0 text--right"><span class="label lg:label--large">{{ round.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" | replace: "–", "&#8288;–&#8288;" }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template race_header %}
{% if inline_flag %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
  <div class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y gap--small">
    {% render "race_flag", race: race, flag_size: flag_size %}
    <span class="title {{ name_size }}">{{ race.name }}</span>
  </div>
  {% if split_dates %}
    {% comment %}The circuit alone, then the round and dates: no line starts or ends on a dot.{% endcomment %}
    {% if race.circuit %}<span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{{ race.circuit }}</span>{% endif %}
    <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">Round&nbsp;{{ race.round }} · {{ race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" | replace: "–", "&#8288;–&#8288;" }}</span>
  {% else %}
    <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{% if race.circuit %}{{ race.circuit }} · {% endif %}Round&nbsp;{{ race.round }} · {{ race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" | replace: "–", "&#8288;–&#8288;" }}</span>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y gap--medium">
  {% render "race_flag", race: race, flag_size: flag_size %}
  <div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
    <span class="title {{ name_size }}">{{ race.name }}</span>
    {% if compact_details %}
      {% comment %}One line in landscape; in portrait the circuit, then the round and dates.{% endcomment %}
      <span class="flex flex--row portrait:flex--col portrait:flex--left gap--none">
        {% if race.circuit %}<span class="label {{ detail_size }}">{{ race.circuit }}<span class="portrait:hidden">&nbsp;·&nbsp;</span></span>{% endif %}
        <span class="label {{ detail_size }}">Round {{ race.round }} · {{ race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" | replace: "–", "&#8288;–&#8288;" }}</span>
      </span>
    {% else %}
      {% if race.circuit %}<span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{{ race.circuit }}</span>{% endif %}
      <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">Round {{ race.round }} · {{ race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" | replace: "–", "&#8288;–&#8288;" }}</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% template race_flag %}
{% comment %}
  Dither flags on both OG and X to the target device's palette.
{% endcomment %}
{% if race.flag_url %}
<div class="bg--black p--0.5 shrink-0 flex">
  <img class="image image-dither shrink-0 w--auto {{ flag_size }}" src="{{ race.flag_url }}" alt="">
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The weekend timeline. `name` picks the row label ("FP1", "Quali"); `short`
  uses the narrow-layout labels ("FP1", "SQ"). `tail` shows the last `limit` rows so the
  narrow layouts keep qualifying and the race. A finished row lists its top
  three, or with `fill` as many drivers as fit on the line. Each row carries its forecast:
  temperature, rain chance when it is worth mentioning, and session rainfall
  (`no_rainfall` drops the last two where the slot is too narrow). `no_next`
  drops the "Next" badge where the lead just above already names that session.
{% endcomment %}
{% template schedule %}
{% if schedule and schedule.size > 0 %}
{% assign schedule_limit = limit | default: 99 %}
{% comment %}
  The full screen packs the name and time columns (`fill`), so they take wider
  padding there; in the halves that pushed the table past the slot. `tight`
  takes less, which buys the portrait OG half its third driver.
{% endcomment %}
{% if fill and aligned %}{% assign schedule_pad = "pr--3" %}{% elsif tight %}{% assign schedule_pad = "pr--1" %}{% else %}{% assign schedule_pad = "pr--2" %}{% endif %}
{% comment %}
  The forecast cells had no padding: at the table's narrowest, "30°C", its
  icon and "45%" touched. `forecast_size` sets their text on the X:
  `label--large` (TRMNL's reviewer chose it: the icon already holds the row's
  height) unless a slot is too narrow for it.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign schedule_forecast_size = forecast_size | default: "lg:label--large" %}
{% if tight %}{% assign schedule_cell_pad = "pr--1" %}{% else %}{% assign schedule_cell_pad = "pr--2" %}{% endif %}
{% assign schedule_offset = 0 %}
{% if tail and schedule.size > schedule_limit %}
  {% assign schedule_offset = schedule.size | minus: schedule_limit %}
{% endif %}
{% assign schedule_rain_column = false %}
{% unless no_rainfall %}
{% for row in schedule limit: schedule_limit offset: schedule_offset %}
  {% if row.state == "upcoming" and row.weather and row.weather.rain != "" %}{% assign schedule_rain_column = true %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endunless %}
{% comment %}Columns after the time: temperature, icon, rain chance?, rainfall?, status?.{% endcomment %}
{% assign schedule_after_time = 2 %}
{% unless no_next %}{% assign schedule_after_time = schedule_after_time | plus: 1 %}{% endunless %}
{% if schedule_rain_column %}{% assign schedule_after_time = schedule_after_time | plus: 1 %}{% endif %}
{% unless no_rainfall %}{% assign schedule_after_time = schedule_after_time | plus: 1 %}{% endunless %}
<table class="table w--full {{ size }}">
  <tbody>
    {% for row in schedule limit: schedule_limit offset: schedule_offset %}
    <tr>
      {% comment %}`pr--2` on the name and time: the narrow OG ran them together ("QualiFri 13:00").{% endcomment %}
      {% comment %}The name cell holds the icon's height, so every row is as tall whatever it carries.{% endcomment %}
      {% comment %}
        With `fill`, the name and time columns shrink to their content (`w--0`;
        a cell never goes narrower than that), so the spare width goes to the
        drivers. The non-breaking space keeps "Sprint Quali" on one line.
      {% endcomment %}
      <td{% if fill %} class="w--0"{% endif %}><span class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y h--[22px] lg:h--[32px]"><span class="title title--small lg:title--base {{ schedule_pad }}">{% if fill %}{{ row[name] | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" }}{% else %}{{ row[name] }}{% endif %}</span></span></td>
      <td{% if fill %} class="w--0"{% endif %}>
        {% if aligned %}
        <span class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y gap--xsmall">
          <span class="label label--base lg:label--large w--[32px] lg:w--[40px] shrink-0">{{ row.weekday }}</span>
          <span class="label label--base lg:label--large {{ schedule_pad }}">{{ row.time }}</span>
        </span>
        {% else %}
        <span class="label label--base lg:label--large {{ schedule_pad }}">{{ row.when | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      {% comment %}
        One column per forecast value, so the table lines them up: a narrower
        temperature ("31°C") moved the icon and rainfall on its own row. Once a
        session has run, its forecast is history: the row shows its leaders,
        or "Awaiting result", across those columns instead. Carrying both
        crushed the narrow layouts ("QualiFri 13:00").
      {% endcomment %}
      {% if row.state != "upcoming" %}
      <td colspan="{{ schedule_after_time }}">
        {% comment %}The icon's height, so a finished row is as tall as one with a forecast.{% endcomment %}
        <span class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y h--[22px] lg:h--[32px]">
        {% if row.state == "done" and fill and row.codes %}
          {% comment %}
            As many drivers as fit, whole codes only, with no script: they
            wrap onto a second line, which the row's height clips
            (`rounded--none` is the Framework's `overflow: hidden`). `w--0
            w--min-full` fills the cell without adding to the table's own
            width calculation, so a long session never squeezes the name and
            time columns.
          {% endcomment %}
          <span class="block w--0 w--min-full h--[22px] lg:h--[32px] rounded--none">
            <span class="flex flex--row flex--wrap flex--left gap--xsmall lg:gap--small">
              {% for code in row.codes %}<span class="flex flex--center-y h--[22px] lg:h--[32px]"><span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ code }}</span></span>{% endfor %}
            </span>
          </span>
        {% elsif row.state == "done" %}
          <span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ row.top3 | join: " " }}</span>
        {% elsif row.state == "awaiting" %}
          {% comment %}One line where there is room; the narrow slot clipped it, so there it may wrap.{% endcomment %}
          <span class="label label--small 2bit:label--gray 4bit:label--gray">{% if no_rainfall %}Awaiting result{% else %}Awaiting&nbsp;result{% endif %}</span>
        {% endif %}
        </span>
      </td>
      {% else %}
      <td class="{{ schedule_cell_pad }}">{% if row.weather %}<span class="label label--small {{ schedule_forecast_size }}">{{ row.weather.temp }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="{{ schedule_cell_pad }}">{% if row.weather %}<img class="image image-dither w--[22px] h--[22px] lg:w--[32px] lg:h--[32px]" src="{{ row.weather.icon }}" alt="">{% endif %}</td>
      {% if schedule_rain_column %}<td class="{{ schedule_cell_pad }}">{% if row.weather and row.weather.rain != "" %}<span class="label label--small {{ schedule_forecast_size }}">{{ row.weather.rain }}</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endif %}
      {% unless no_rainfall %}<td class="{{ schedule_cell_pad }}">{% if row.weather %}<span class="label label--small {{ schedule_forecast_size }}">{{ row.weather.rainAmount | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" }}</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endunless %}
      {% unless no_next %}<td>{% if row.next %}<span class="label label--small lg:label--base label--filled">Next</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endunless %}
      {% endif %}
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}


{% comment %}
  `headline_size` is always passed. It is not called `size`: liquidjs, which
  renders the /trmnl page, resolves a missing `size` to 0 where TRMNL's Ruby
  Liquid falls back to a default, so the page and the device disagreed.
{% endcomment %}
{% template news %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall {% if fill or news.size == 0 %}h--full{% endif %} {% if news.size == 0 %}flex--center{% elsif fill %}flex--left flex--center-y{% endif %}" data-overflow="true">
  {% if news.size == 0 %}<span class="label label--small {{ empty_size | default: 'lg:label--base' }}">No news yet.</span>{% endif %}
  {% for item in news limit: limit %}
  <div class="item">
    <div class="meta"></div>
    <div class="content">
      <span class="title {{ headline_size }}" data-clamp="{{ clamp | default: 2 }}">{{ item.headline }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% unless forloop.last %}<div class="divider divider--h"></div>{% endunless %}
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  A session result, up to `limit` rows. `split` lays ten rows out as two
  columns of five, where one column of ten would not fit. Both are always
  passed.

  Split by hand, not by TRMNL's overflow engine (`data-overflow-max-cols` on
  one `.column`), which TRMNL's rules prefer. Tried on 23 September 2026: the
  engine fills the first column before starting the second, so ten rows came
  out 7 + 3 on the OG and 9 + 1 on the X, and on a portrait X it clipped the
  list after eight names. TRMNL's own guide warns the engine is unpredictable
  on e-ink.
{% endcomment %}
{% template result %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small">
  <span class="title title--small {% if compact %}lg:title--base{% else %}lg:title--large{% endif %}">{{ result.label }}</span>
  {% if split and result.rows.size > 5 %}
  <div class="columns">
    <div class="column">{% render "result_rows", rows: result.rows, limit: 5, offset: 0, compact: compact %}</div>
    <div class="column">{% render "result_rows", rows: result.rows, limit: 5, offset: 5, compact: compact %}</div>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  {% render "result_rows", rows: result.rows, limit: limit, offset: 0, compact: compact %}
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template result_rows %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small">
  {% for row in rows limit: limit offset: offset %}
  <div class="item">
    <div class="meta"><span class="index">{% if row.status != "" %}{{ row.status }}{% else %}{{ row.pos }}{% endif %}</span></div>
    <div class="content">
      <span class="title title--small {% if compact %}lg:title--base{% else %}lg:title--large{% endif %}">{{ row.name }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template grid %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small">
  <span class="title title--small lg:title--base">Starting grid</span>
  {% assign half = grid.size | plus: 1 | divided_by: 2 %}
  <div class="columns">
    <div class="column">{% render "grid_rows", rows: grid, limit: half, offset: 0 %}</div>
    <div class="column">{% render "grid_rows", rows: grid, limit: half, offset: half %}</div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  `lg:portrait:table--xsmall`: stacked under the timeline on a portrait X,
  eleven rows per column need the same compact height as the OG.
{% endcomment %}
{% template grid_rows %}
<table class="table table--xsmall lg:table--base lg:portrait:table--xsmall">
  <tbody>
    {% for row in rows limit: limit offset: offset %}
    <tr>
      <td><span class="label label--small">{{ row.pos }}</span></td>
      <td><span class="title title--small">{{ row.code }}</span></td>
      <td><span class="label label--small 2bit:label--gray 4bit:label--gray">{{ row.note }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The way from the screen to the site, the same on every layout. `url` is the
  race's, or the standings' in the off-season. The link is the short /t/ form
  and carries
  utm_source=trmnl, utm_medium=qr and the screen phase as utm_content, for
  PostHog. 2px modules at error-correction level M leave room for content
  in the smaller layouts.
{% endcomment %}
{% template qr %}
{% if size_class %}
  {% capture qr_class %}class="qr-code {{ size_class }}"{% endcapture %}
{% else %}
  {% assign qr_class = 'class="qr-code"' %}
{% endif %}
{% capture qr_markup %}{{ url | qr_code: 2, "m" }}{% endcapture %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--center">
  {{ qr_markup | replace: 'class="qr-code"', qr_class }}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The lead session's own forecast under the lead, one format everywhere:
  temperature · icon and condition · rain chance, when worth mentioning ·
  wind beside its own icon, sized to match. `rain_amount` adds the session's
  rainfall where no timeline carries it (the quarter), unless it is "Dry",
  which only repeated the condition ("Clear · Dry").

  Two groups, so a narrow slot breaks between them and never leaves a dot at
  the end of a line: `stack` names the breakpoint ("portrait:") at which the
  second group drops below the first and the dot between them goes.
  `no_wind` leaves the wind out where even two lines do not fit. The X in
  portrait once put them back on one line, which a long forecast could not
  fit: the wind wrapped inside itself ("NE 11 / km/h").
{% endcomment %}
{% template lead_weather %}
{% if weather %}
{% assign weather_text = text_size | default: 'lg:label--base' %}
{% assign weather_more = false %}
{% assign weather_wind = weather.wind %}
{% if no_wind %}{% assign weather_wind = "" %}{% endif %}
{% if weather.rain != "" or weather_wind != "" %}{% assign weather_more = true %}{% endif %}
{% if rain_amount and weather.rainAmount != "Dry" %}{% assign weather_more = true %}{% endif %}
<span class="flex flex--row flex--center flex--center-y gap--small{% if stack %} {{ stack }}flex--col {{ stack }}gap--xsmall{% endif %}">
  <span class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--small">
    <span class="label label--small {{ weather_text }}">{{ weather.temp }}</span>
    <span class="label label--small {{ weather_text }}" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
    <span class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--xsmall">
      <img class="image image-dither w--[24px] h--[24px] lg:w--[32px] lg:h--[32px]" src="{{ weather.icon }}" alt="">
      <span class="label label--small {{ weather_text }}">{{ weather.condition }}</span>
    </span>
  </span>
  {% if weather_more %}
  <span class="label label--small {{ weather_text }}{% if stack %} {{ stack }}hidden{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
  <span class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--small">
    {% assign weather_first = true %}
    {% if weather.rain != "" %}
    <span class="label label--small {{ weather_text }}">{{ weather.rain }}</span>
    {% assign weather_first = false %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if rain_amount and weather.rainAmount != "Dry" %}
    {% unless weather_first %}<span class="label label--small {{ weather_text }}" aria-hidden="true">·</span>{% endunless %}
    <span class="label label--small {{ weather_text }}">{{ weather.rainAmount }}</span>
    {% assign weather_first = false %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if weather_wind != "" %}
    {% unless weather_first %}<span class="label label--small {{ weather_text }}" aria-hidden="true">·</span>{% endunless %}
    <span class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--xsmall">
      <svg class="w--[24px] h--[24px] lg:w--[32px] lg:h--[32px]" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="#000" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 7h12a3 3 0 1 0-3-3"/><path d="M2 12h17a3 3 0 1 1-3 3"/><path d="M4 17h7a2 2 0 1 1-2 2"/></g></svg>
      <span class="label label--small {{ weather_text }}">{{ weather.wind }}</span>
    </span>
    {% endif %}
  </span>
  {% endif %}
</span>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The off-season screen: the season just run. `standings.title` is "Formula 1
  2026 Standings" and `standings.detail` "After 23 rounds"; before the
  season ends (only the /trmnl page shows it then) they say so instead.
{% endcomment %}
{% template standings_header %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
  <span class="title {{ title_size }}">{{ standings.title }}</span>
  <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{{ standings.detail }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}The champion, as the lead: "2026 champion", then the name.{% endcomment %}
{% template leader %}
{% if standings.drivers.first.name != blank %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall w--full">
  <span class="title lg:title--large">{{ standings.leader_label }}</span>
  <span class="value {{ value_size }}" data-value-fit="true">{{ standings.drivers.first.name }}</span>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  One championship table, drivers or constructors: position, name, points.
  `label`, `limit`, `offset` and `size` are always passed. An empty label
  leaves the second driver column aligned below the shared heading.
{% endcomment %}
{% template standings_table %}
{% if rows and rows.size > 0 %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall">
  {% if label != "" %}<span class="title title--small lg:title--base w--full">{{ label }}</span>{% endif %}
  <table class="table {{ size }}">
    <tbody>
      {% for row in rows limit: limit offset: offset %}
      <tr>
        <td><span class="label label--small">{{ row.pos }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="title title--small">{{ row.name }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="label label--small">{{ row.points }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The drivers' championship in the full screen's news column, while the
  build-up has no headlines: every driver, by three-letter code, split into
  `cols` columns so the whole table fits. Sized to match the timeline beside it.
  Positions read "P1" so they are not mistaken for the points beside them:
  in four columns one column's points sat next to the next one's position.
  A rule between columns does the same job between the tables.
{% endcomment %}
{% template championship %}
{% assign per_column = rows.size | plus: cols | minus: 1 | divided_by: cols %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--small w--full">
  <span class="title lg:title--large">Drivers' Championship</span>
  <div class="flex flex--row flex--top gap--medium w--full">
    {% for column in (1..cols) %}
    {% assign column_offset = column | minus: 1 | times: per_column %}
    {% unless forloop.first %}<div class="w--[1px] self--stretch shrink-0 bg--black"></div>{% endunless %}
    <div class="grow">
      <table class="table w--full {{ size }}">
        <tbody>
          {% for row in rows limit: per_column offset: column_offset %}
          <tr>
            <td><span class="label label--small lg:label--base w--[28px] lg:w--[44px]">P{{ row.pos }}</span></td>
            <td class="w--full"><span class="title title--small lg:title--base">{{ row.code }}</span></td>
            <td class="text--right"><span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ row.points }}</span></td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The checkered band under the full screen's lead.
{% endcomment %}
{% template checker %}
{% comment %}
  This template is entirely static and needs no variables from its caller.
  A whole number of squares scaled to the column, so the band never ends
  on a cut square. An odd count puts a black square in both top corners;
  the height follows the width so the squares stay square. Portrait's
  full-width column takes more of them, or the band grows to 58px on an X.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="w--full portrait:hidden" aria-hidden="true">
  <svg class="block h--auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 376 16" width="100%" shape-rendering="crispEdges" role="presentation">
    <defs><pattern id="schedule-checker" width="16" height="16" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><rect width="8" height="8" fill="#000"/><rect x="8" width="8" height="8" fill="#fff"/><rect y="8" width="8" height="8" fill="#fff"/><rect x="8" y="8" width="8" height="8" fill="#000"/></pattern></defs>
    <rect width="376" height="16" fill="url(#schedule-checker)"/>
  </svg>
</div>
<div class="w--full hidden portrait:block" aria-hidden="true">
  <svg class="block h--auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 472 16" width="100%" shape-rendering="crispEdges" role="presentation">
    <defs><pattern id="schedule-checker-portrait" width="16" height="16" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><rect width="8" height="8" fill="#000"/><rect x="8" width="8" height="8" fill="#fff"/><rect y="8" width="8" height="8" fill="#fff"/><rect x="8" y="8" width="8" height="8" fill="#000"/></pattern></defs>
    <rect width="472" height="16" fill="url(#schedule-checker-portrait)"/>
  </svg>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The whole race classification once the weekend is over, in two columns, by
  code with "P1" positions, as the championship reads, and the official gap
  (the winner's race time, then "+0.196", "+1 lap"). A driver who did not
  finish shows "DNF", "DNS" or "DSQ" in place of a position, so the tail of
  the list does not read as finishing places.
{% endcomment %}
{% template classification %}
{% assign per_column = result.rows.size | plus: 1 | divided_by: 2 %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--small w--full">
  <span class="title lg:title--large">{{ result.label }}</span>
  <div class="flex flex--row flex--top gap--medium w--full">
    {% for column in (1..2) %}
    {% assign column_offset = column | minus: 1 | times: per_column %}
    {% unless forloop.first %}<div class="w--[1px] self--stretch shrink-0 bg--black"></div>{% endunless %}
    <div class="grow">
      <table class="table w--full {{ size }}">
        <tbody>
          {% for row in result.rows limit: per_column offset: column_offset %}
          <tr>
            <td><span class="label label--small lg:label--base w--[28px] lg:w--[44px]">{% if row.status != "" %}{{ row.status }}{% else %}P{{ row.pos }}{% endif %}</span></td>
            <td class="w--full"><span class="title title--small lg:title--base">{{ row.code }}</span></td>
            <td class="text--right"><span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ row.gap }}</span></td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  When the next round is on, under the finished weekend's news: its flag,
  name and dates.
{% endcomment %}
{% template next_race %}
{% comment %}
  A small race header: the flag beside "Next race · 2 – 4 Oct" and, under
  it, the name. Two short lines, so the column keeps room for another headline.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y gap--small w--full">
  {% render "race_flag", race: next_race, flag_size: "h--[28px] w--max-[56px] lg:h--[56px] lg:w--max-[112px] lg:portrait:h--[44px] lg:portrait:w--max-[88px]" %}
  <div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
    <span class="label label--small lg:label--base">Next race · {{ next_race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" | replace: "–", "&#8288;–&#8288;" }}</span>
    <span class="title title--small lg:title--large">{{ next_race.name }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The icon is inline, as TRMNL's guide asks: a URL can fail to load when the
  screen is drawn. Captured inside the template because a rendered template
  cannot see variables from outside it.
{% endcomment %}
{% template title_bar %}
{%- capture icon -%}<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="24" height="24"><g fill="#000" transform="translate(16 16) skewX(-12) translate(-16 -16)"><rect x="5" y="13" width="6" height="12"/><rect x="14" y="7" width="6" height="18"/><rect x="23" y="16" width="6" height="9"/></g></svg>{%- endcapture -%}
<div class="title_bar">
  <img class="image image-dither image-stroke" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,{{ icon | base64_encode }}" alt="">
  <span class="title">GrandPrixPicks.com</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}
